# Stellar Component Library Rules for Svelte

## Overview
The Stellar component library provides a comprehensive set of UI components and styles for spacecraft operation tools, with first-class support for Svelte applications.

## Installation

```bash
npm install @nasa-jpl/stellar-svelte @nasa-jpl/stellar --save
```

## Import Patterns

### 1. Svelte Components
Import pre-built Svelte components from the Stellar Svelte package:

```typescript
// Basic components
import { Button, Input, Label, Select } from '@nasa-jpl/stellar-svelte';

// Example usage
<Button variant="ghost" size="xs">Click me</Button>
<Input type="text" placeholder="Enter value" />
```

### 2. Icons
Import icons using the `?component` suffix (required for Vite):

```typescript
// Single icon import
import CheckIcon from '@nasa-jpl/stellar/icons/check.svg?component';

// Common icon imports
import WarningIcon from '@nasa-jpl/stellar/icons/warning.svg?component';
import ArrowLeftIcon from '@nasa-jpl/stellar/icons/arrow_left.svg?component';
import CloseIcon from '@nasa-jpl/stellar/icons/close.svg?component';
import SearchIcon from '@nasa-jpl/stellar/icons/search.svg?component';

// Example usage
<CheckIcon />
<WarningIcon class="red-icon" />
```

### 3. Required CSS Imports
Add these imports to your global CSS file (e.g., `app.css`):

```css
/* Stellar Svelte theme and font */
@import '@nasa-jpl/stellar-svelte/theme';
@import '@nasa-jpl/stellar-svelte/font';

/* Core Stellar styles */
@import '@nasa-jpl/stellar/css/variables.css';
@import '@nasa-jpl/stellar/css/typography.css';
@import '@nasa-jpl/stellar/css/button.css';
@import '@nasa-jpl/stellar/css/input.css';
@import '@nasa-jpl/stellar/css/select.css';
@import '@nasa-jpl/stellar/css/badge.css';
```

### 4. Tailwind Integration
If using Tailwind CSS, configure it to work with Stellar:

```javascript
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  content: [
    './node_modules/@nasa-jpl/stellar-svelte/dist/**/*.{html,js,svelte,ts}',
    './src/**/*.{html,js,svelte,ts}'
  ],
  presets: [
    require('@nasa-jpl/stellar-svelte/tailwindConfig')
  ]
};
```

## Common Component Usage

### Basic Components
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { Button, Input, Label, Select } from '@nasa-jpl/stellar-svelte';
  import type { FieldStore } from '../types/form';

  export let field: FieldStore<any>;
  export let disabled: boolean = false;
</script>

<div class="form-field">
  <Label for="myInput">Input Label</Label>
  <Input
    type="text"
    id="myInput"
    disabled={disabled}
    bind:value={field.value}
  />
</div>
```

### Menu Components
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { Menu, MenuItem } from '@nasa-jpl/stellar-svelte';
  import CheckIcon from '@nasa-jpl/stellar/icons/check.svg?component';
</script>

<Menu>
  <MenuItem>
    <CheckIcon />
    <span>Menu Item</span>
  </MenuItem>
</Menu>
```

### Progress Indicators
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { ProgressRadial } from '@nasa-jpl/stellar-svelte';
</script>

<ProgressRadial
  useBackground={false}
  size={14}
/>
```

## Best Practices

1. **TypeScript Usage**
   - Always use `<script lang="ts">` for better type safety
   - Import types from Stellar when available

2. **Icon Handling**
   - Always append `?component` to icon imports
   - Use semantic class names for icon colors (e.g., `red-icon`, `warning-icon`)

3. **Component Props**
   - Provide default values for optional props
   - Document prop types using TypeScript interfaces

4. **CSS Classes**
   - Use Stellar's built-in classes with `st-` prefix
   - Combine with Tailwind classes when needed

